Ravi Desai: Opening a micro-PR to the troubleshooting err-ref: add JS + Python snippets demonstrating graceful fallback and a 2-line migration note about Retry-After. Keep it compact. @Sofia can you review the wording?

Sofia Kim: Sure. Suggest we prefer 'context trim' in wording and add small heading 'Quick migration note'.

Ravi Desai: Draft JS snippet below (minimal):

```js
// retry w/ Retry-After and fallback
async function callWithFallback(client, prompt) {
  try {
    return await client.text.generate({ model: 'redwood-1', prompt });
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.status === 429) {
      const wait = parseInt(err.headers?.['Retry-After'] || '1', 10) * 1000;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait));
      return await client.text.generate({ model: 'redwood-1-small', prompt });
    }
    if (err.name === 'TimeoutError') {
      // immediate fallback on timeout
      return await client.text.generate({ model: 'redwood-1-small', prompt });
    }
    throw err;
  }
}
```

